steps.message:
The last run has finished, and the account of it is to be seen in the file. What is to be gathered from it has already been made partly plain in the other list. The lowest limit, that is to say the feet, went on rising up from the 50th to the 71st of the numbered instances. Then in the next it is to be found that this has been brought to a close. It is in that neighborhood that the moment of alighting is to be sought, while the moment of the leaving off is to be had a little before the 54th. To fix these with exactness the several numbers must be compared with one another. The very next step is to bring to an end the work that is now in hand, so that the account may be set down as is required.

{
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '45,75p' track.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

The result that has now been brought to view is to be found in the numbers 56 and 117. In the account of the instances that had been had in readiness these were to be found as the 59th and the 72nd. The means of the difference is to be seen in that the several instances that are to be had after the movement had been made are to be looked upon by the present course of procedure. This is in a manner that is to be trusted in any instance in which the same manner of movement is to be had. The person in the act of running in the part after the movement will in the end be found to bring about the coming to a stop that is to be looked for in the same manner as that in which the leaving off had been brought about.

It is to be had as the end of this matter that the working be set down in the form in which it has now come to pass. The course of procedure that has been had in view is to be found in the file that has been put in the place in which the same is to be sought. And this is to be reckoned as having in the end come to that which was to be had.

